  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour incident reporting and 48-hour customer notice for all thermal incidents. S2 sets a 55°C test and a 5% review threshold but no automatic sales ban, with numerical results to customers but not the public. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit with feasibility escape; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months or approved equivalent; S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with prompt customer notice."
